  "reason": "Evidence: RNA is the dominant signal (image-only acc=0.208; RNA-only multiprofile avgpool=0.591 is close to the best multimodal result of 0.619), and multiprofile+avgpool is the strongest setting so far. However, we have only tested PCA-2000 as the RNA encoder—a linear projection—across all 7 completed experiments. The RNA encoder is the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact design axis remaining. Question: config_005 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_002 (same setting but PCA-2000), isolating whether a learned generative representation (scvi) captures more predictive structure than PCA. Why this is the best use of the next experiment: it directly tests the most consequential unexplored axis (RNA representation quality) without confounding from image modality, fusion, or aggregation changes. If scvi_n200 improves RNA-only performance, we gain a strong prior for deploying it in the multimodal multiprofile setting; if not, PCA remains validated and we can redirect budget toward image encoder or other axes. This maximizes information per experiment under the limited budget."
}

